{"name":"Topiary Tint","hex":"#bbc9b2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"topiary","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, or relating to art of topiaries.","Of a tree or shrub, trimmed in artistic shape."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Art or practice of trimming shrubs or trees in artistic or ornamental shapes, e.g. of animals.","A garden decorated with such art."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/topiary"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Topiary","blocks":[{"text":"Topiary is the horticultural practice of training perennial plants by clipping the foliage and twigs of trees, shrubs and subshrubs to develop and maintain clearly defined shapes, whether geometric or fanciful. The term also refers to plants which have been shaped in this way. As an art form it is a type of living sculpture. The word derives from the Latin word for an ornamental landscape gardener, topiarius, a creator of topia or \"places\", a Greek word that Romans also applied to fictive indoor landscapes executed in fresco."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Cementerio%2C_Tulc%C3%A1n%2C_Ecuador%2C_2015-07-21%2C_DD_60.JPG/330px-Cementerio%2C_Tulc%C3%A1n%2C_Ecuador%2C_2015-07-21%2C_DD_60.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topiary","wikidata":"Q1437791"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Pt-ctb-jardimpaco.jpg/250px-Pt-ctb-jardimpaco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6b/Pt-ctb-jardimpaco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Pt-ctb-jardimpaco.jpg/250px-Pt-ctb-jardimpaco.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Castelo Branco Portugal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APt-ctb-jardimpaco.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Korea-Geoje-Oedo_4098-06.JPG/500px-Korea-Geoje-Oedo_4098-06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Korea-Geoje-Oedo_4098-06.JPG/500px-Korea-Geoje-Oedo_4098-06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cloud-pruning only distantly related to natural forms in Hallyeo Haesang National Park, Geoje, South Korea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKorea-Geoje-Oedo_4098-06.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Hortus_Palatinus_und_Heidelberger_Schloss_von_Jacques_Fouquiere.jpg/500px-Hortus_Palatinus_und_Heidelberger_Schloss_von_Jacques_Fouquiere.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Hortus_Palatinus_und_Heidelber